## 🧠 1. Lower the friction (most important)

- Keep **one main repo** always open (your “daily driver”)
- Predefine tasks → no thinking required when you sit down
- Examples:
    - Improve README
    - Refactor 1 function
    - Add 1 test
    - Fix 1 bug

👉 Goal: *“1 small commit per day” becomes trivial*

---

## ⏱️ 2. Use a fixed daily slot (habit > motivation)

- Same time every day (e.g. 9:00–9:30)
- Treat like brushing teeth
- Even **5–10 min counts**

---

## 🔁 3. Create “evergreen” projects

Have projects that never “end”:

- AI experiments (RAG, agents, etc.)
- Notes repo (markdown knowledge base)
- Leetcode-style repo
- Blog/content repo

👉 You always have somewhere to commit

---

## 🧩 4. Break work into micro-commits

Bad:

- “Build full feature”

Good:

- “Create schema”
- “Add endpoint”
- “Write test”
- “Fix edge case”

👉 Each = 1 commit = 1 green square

---

## 🤖 5. Automate when possible (smart, not fake)

- Scheduled jobs (e.g. daily data pull, cron jobs)
- Bots updating datasets / README stats
- CI pipelines generating artifacts

⚠️ Avoid fake commits just to fill graph → recruiters notice

---

## 📦 6. Use private repos strategically

- GitHub counts **private contributions**
- Work on real stuff (client, experiments, notes)

👉 Clean public profile + consistent graph

---

## 🧪 7. Tie contributions to your career

Given your AI Engineer path:

- Build:
    - RAG system repo
    - Agent framework experiments
    - Prompt engineering playground
    - Evaluation (RAGAS, DeepEval)

👉 Each iteration = commit

---

## 📊 8. Track streaks (simple KPI)

- Define: **“≥1 commit/day”**
- Use tools like:
    - GitHub built-in graph
    - Streak trackers (optional)

---

## 🧹 9. Batch on busy days

- If no time:
    - Commit notes
    - Update docs
    - Push WIP code

👉 Consistency > perfection

---

## 🔥 10. Have a fallback rule

If you're tired:

- Just:
    - Update README
    - Add TODO
    - Rename variables
    - Commit learning notes

👉 Never break the chain

---

## 💡 Simple system (recommended)

- 1 main repo (AI experiments)
- 1 notes repo (daily learnings)
- 15 min daily block
- Minimum: 1 commit/day